# WRONG verdict reproducer: algebraic folding defeats ftz operand flushing.
# README: "equiv F G ftz flushes subnormals: every float operation ... reads
# a subnormal operand as the zero of its sign".  A non-folded multiply does
# flush (mul3 == fl3 under ftz), but x*1 is folded to a bare bitcast, so its
# subnormal operand is never flushed and mul1 still differs from fl under
# ftz (wrong: it should be equal).  Consequently "mul1 == passthru under ftz"
# is an unsound 'equal'.

fl(x: u32) = asfloat(x) > f32(-2^(-126)) && asfloat(x) < f32(2^(-126)) ? f32(0) : asfloat(x)
mul1(x: u32) = asfloat(x) * f32(1)
passthru(x: u32) = asfloat(x)
mul3(x: u32) = asfloat(x) * f32(3)
fl3(x: u32) = fl(x) * f32(3)

equiv mul1 passthru noftz
equiv mul1 passthru ftz
equiv mul1 fl noftz
equiv mul1 fl ftz
equiv mul3 fl3 noftz
equiv mul3 fl3 ftz
